  "name": "engine-sim",
  "description": "A high-performance real-time internal combustion engine simulator designed for high-fidelity audio synthesis and mechanical response emulation. The system models discrete components including pistons, crankshafts, and valvetrains while simulating complex gas dynamics and combustion thermodynamics to produce procedurally generated engine acoustics. It features a custom domain-specific scripting language for engine configuration and a constraint-based physics solver for mechanical linkages.",
